# Component Figma traceability

This rule applies to component pages in `docs/components/` (excluding `overview.md`).

## Required frontmatter contract

Component docs must include this metadata block:

```md
---
doc_type: component
doc_status: draft # draft | ready | needs-review
figma:
  file_url: "https://www.figma.com/design/<file>/<name>?node-id=<node>"
  page: "<FigmaPageName>"
  component: "<ComponentOrSetName>"
  last_verified: "YYYY-MM-DD"
---
```

If a value is unknown, use `TBD` instead of guessing.

## Traceability rules

- `figma.component` must use a human-readable component/set name, not node IDs.
- `figma.page` should match the page name in Figma.
- `figma.last_verified` records the latest manual verification date.
- Keep a direct source link in `## Overview` (human-readable URL text is fine).

## Prohibited values

- Do not use `VariableID:*` as metadata.
- Do not store node IDs as standalone identifiers in tables or prose.
